From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NomDeTom <nomdetom@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: allow the wiphy to move into another network namespace

Without WIPHY_FLAG_NETNS_OK, 'iw phy <phy> set netns ...' is refused
with EOPNOTSUPP, so the interface can't be used from a network
namespace (as test rigs do to pair two radios in one machine).

The driver keeps nothing per namespace. Its only uses of init_net are
in two optional parts, both off in the default build: the bridge
extension (CONFIG_BR_SUPPORT) looks its bridge up by name in init_net,
and band steering (CONFIG_BAND_STEERING) keeps its netlink socket
there. So the flag is set only when neither is built in.

The same change, with the gate by Shen Mintao, is merged in
shenmintao/aic8800d80 as 2e305e8 and 051b623 (#114).
---
 src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -9226,6 +9226,11 @@
         WIPHY_FLAG_4ADDR_STATION |
         WIPHY_FLAG_4ADDR_AP;
 
+#if !defined(CONFIG_BR_SUPPORT) && !defined(CONFIG_BAND_STEERING)
+    /* The optional bridge and steering paths still use init_net. */
+    wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_NETNS_OK;
+#endif
+
     #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 16, 0)
     wiphy->max_num_csa_counters = BCN_MAX_CSA_CPT;
     #endif
